Now chunk C: UI state, audio, actions, input, touch, animation, resize, kickoff.

Need careful ordering: `playing`, `locked`, `started`, `selectedType` declared with `let`. Functions reference. `toast` function declaration.

UI elements query. overlay etc.

Start:
```js
const overlay = document.getElementById('overlay');
const startBtn = document.getElementById('startBtn');
const resetBtn = document.getElementById('resetBtn');
...
let playing=false, locked=false, started=false, selectedType=1, muted=false;
let lastTime = performance.now();
let bobPhase=0;
```

selectSlot:
```js
const slotEls = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.slot'));
function selectSlot(index){
 const id = index+1;
 if (id<1||id>8) return;
 selectedType=id;
 slotEls.forEach((el,i)=>{ el.classList.toggle('active', i===index); el.setAttribute('aria-pressed', i===index ? 'true':'false'); });
 sfx('select');
}
```
Keyboard selection uses index. Click uses `Number(dataset.id)-1`.

`beginPlay`:
```js
function beginPlay(){
 started=true;
 overlay.classList.add('hidden');
 overlay.classList.remove('paused');
 initAudio();
 if (isCoarse) {
   playing=true;
   document.body.classList.add('playing');
   return;
 }
 if (!locked && renderer.domElement.requestPointerLock) {
   try { renderer.domElement.requestPointerLock(); } catch(e) {}
 }
}
```
After requesting lock, playing becomes true on change. But if lock works, fine.

Potential issue: mobile page might still be classified not touch by matchMedia in playwright. We'll test with hasTouch.

`showPause`:
```js
function showPause(){
 overlay.classList.remove('hidden');
 overlay.classList.add('paused');
 startBtn.textContent='Devam Et';
 started = true;
}
```
The overlay title remains VOXEL DÜNYA. Could change eyebrow/sub? Not needed. Add overlay mode. Maybe add `#pauseTitle`? The overlay has h1 static. Could update `h1` text to "DURAKLATILDI"? Then the brand disappears. Instead update `.eyebrow` text? Let's add `const eyebrow = document.querySelector('.eyebrow')` and set "Oyun duraklatıldı" on pause, "3D Voxel Sandbox" on start. And sub? Keep. Fine.

But on pause the startBtn text "Devam Et", reset visible. Good. On initial load, reset hidden (CSS default display none; only .paused shows).

Pointer lock change:
```js
document.addEventListener('pointerlockchange', () => {
 const nowLocked = document.pointerLockElement === renderer.domElement;
 if (nowLocked) {
   locked = true; playing = true; started = true;
   overlay.classList.add('hidden');
   document.body.classList.add('playing');
 } else {
   const wasLocked = locked;
   locked = false;
   if (wasLocked && !isCoarse) {
     playing = false;
     keys.clear();
     touchInput.x = touchInput.y = 0;
     document.body.classList.remove('playing');
     showPause();
   }
 }
});
```
If pointer lock exits unexpectedly, show pause. `started` guard.

Pointer lock error:
```js
document.addEventListener('pointerlockerror', () => {
 toast('Fare kilidi açılamadı. Sahneye tıklayıp tekrar dene.');
});
```
No overlay show.

Canvas pointerdown desktop:
```js
renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {
 if (isCoarse) return;
 if (!locked && started) beginPlay();
});
```
But when overlay hidden and not locked, this triggers. When overlay visible, overlay covers canvas, so no.

Mouse look:
```js
document.addEventListener('mousemove', e => {
 if (!locked || !playing) return;
 yaw -= e.movementX * 0.0022;
 pitch = clamp(pitch - e.movementY * 0.0022, -1.45, 1.45);
});
```

Mouse buttons:
```js
document.addEventListener('mousedown', e => {
 if (isCoarse || !locked || !playing) return;
 if (e.button === 0) breakTarget();
 else if (e.button === 2) placeBlock();
});
document.addEventListener('contextmenu', e => e.preventDefault());
```
Right-click on canvas also context menu suppressed.

Touch look on canvas:
```js
let lookPointer=null, lookX=0, lookY=0;
renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {
 if (!isCoarse || !playing) return;
 if (e.pointerType !== 'touch' && e.pointerType !== 'pen') return;
 if (lookPointer !== null) return;
 lookPointer = e.pointerId; lookX=e.clientX; lookY=e.clientY;
 try { renderer.domElement.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch{}
});
...
```
Note if `isCoarse` false but user touches a touchscreen laptop, touch UI isn't shown. Fine.

Joystick and buttons even if body has touch class but isCoarse false? class set from isCoarse. fine.

Keyboard:
```js
window.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
 if (e.code === 'KeyM') { toggleMute(); return; }
 if (!playing) return;
 if (e.code === 'Space') { e.preventDefault(); wantJump = true; }
 if (e.code === 'KeyW' || ... ) { keys.add(e.code); }
 if (e.code.startsWith('Digit')) { const n = Number(e.code.slice(5)); if (n>=1&&n<=8) selectSlot(n-1); }
 if (e.code === 'KeyR') resetWorld();
});
```
Careful Digit code slice: 'Digit1'.slice(5) => '1'? "Digit1" indices: D0 i1 g2 i3 t4 1=5 -> yes '1'. Good.
Prevent default for digits? no. Prevent for Space. Also `e.repeat` for R reset repeated -> guard `!e.repeat`.
Keyup remove.
When playing false but M works (mute) good.
Escape handled by browser. If overlay showing and user presses Enter/Space? Not needed.

`resetWorld`:
```js
function resetWorld(){
 clearWorld();
 generateWorld();
 particles.forEach(p=>scene.remove(p)); particles.length=0;
 respawn(false);
 toast('Dünya yenilendi 🌍');
 sfx('place');
}
```
Also if on pause, after reset maybe keep overlay. R during play resets.

Actions:
```js
function breakTarget(){
 const hit = currentTarget;
 if (!hit) return;
 const u = hit.object.userData;
 if (u.y <= 0) { toast('Ana kaya kırılamaz'); sfx('deny'); return; }
 removeBlockAt(u.x,u.y,u.z);
 burst(u.x+.5,u.y+.5,u.z+.5,u.type);
 currentTarget=null; highlight.visible=false;
 sfx('break');
}
```
Use `toast` with throttle? fine.

Place:
```js
function placeBlock(){
 const hit=currentTarget; if(!hit) return;
 const n=hit.face.normal;
 const x=hit.object.userData.x + Math.round(n.x);
 ...
 if (blockMap.has(keyOf(x,y,z))) return;
 if (y<0 || y>48) { toast('Daha yükseğe koyamazsın'); return; }
 if (blockHitsPlayer(x,y,z)) { toast('Buraya sığmıyor'); sfx('deny'); return; }
 addBlock(x,y,z,selectedType,true);
 sfx('place');
}
```
Note: hit.face could be null? For raycast mesh hit it's set. Use optional check.
Round normal only values ±1. Good.

Audio:
```js
let audioCtx=null, muted=false;
function initAudio(){
 if (!audioCtx) { try { audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext||window.webkitAudioContext)(); } catch(e) { audioCtx=null; } }
 if (audioCtx && audioCtx.state === 'suspended') audioCtx.resume().catch(()=>{});
}
function tone(f0,f1,dur,type,vol){
 if (!audioCtx || muted || audioCtx.state !== 'running') return;
 const t=audioCtx.currentTime;
 const o=audioCtx.createOscillator(), g=audioCtx.createGain();
 o.type=type; o.frequency.setValueAtTime(f0,t);
 o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(Math.max(25,f1), t+dur);
 g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001,t);
 g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(vol,t+0.008);
 g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001,t+dur);
 o.connect(g); g.connect(audioCtx.destination);
 o.start(t); o.stop(t+dur+0.03);
}
function sfx(kind){
 switch(kind){
  case 'break': tone(190,70,.13,'square',.035); break;
  case 'place': tone(130,220,.08,'sine',.05); break;
  case 'jump': tone(300,440,.11,'sine',.025); break;
  case 'select': tone(520,620,.05,'sine',.018); break;
  case 'deny': tone(120,80,.1,'sawtooth',.025); break;
 }
}
function toggleMute(){
 muted=!muted;
 toast(muted ? 'Ses kapatıldı' : 'Ses açıldı');
 if (!muted) { initAudio(); sfx('select'); }
}
```
Note: AudioContext creation on page load? Only beginPlay. M before starting gets toggle; fine.

Toast:
```js
let toastTimer=0;
const toastEl=document.getElementById('toast');
function toast(msg){
 toastEl.textContent=msg;
 toastEl.classList.add('show');
 clearTimeout(toastTimer);
 toastTimer=setTimeout(()=>toastEl.classList.remove('show'),1500);
}
```

Joystick:
```js
const joy = document.getElementById('joystick');
const knob = document.getElementById('knob');
let joyPointer=null;
function joyMove(e){
 const r=joy.getBoundingClientRect();
 const cx=r.left+r.width/2, cy=r.top+r.height/2;
 let dx=e.clientX-cx, dy=e.clientY-cy;
 const max=r.width*0.34;
 const len=Math.hypot(dx,dy);
 if (len>max) { dx=dx/len*max; dy=dy/len*max; }
 knob.style.transform = `translate(${dx}px, ${dy}px)`;
 touchInput.x = dx/max;
 touchInput.y = -dy/max;
}
joy.addEventListener('pointerdown', e=>{ e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); if(joyPointer!==null) return; joyPointer=e.pointerId; joy.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); joyMove(e); });
joy.addEventListener('pointermove', e=>{ if(e.pointerId!==joyPointer) return; e.preventDefault(); joyMove(e); });
function joyEnd(e){ if(e.pointerId!==joyPointer) return; joyPointer=null; touchInput.x=0; touchInput.y=0; knob.style.transform='translate(0,0)'; }
joy.addEventListener('pointerup', joyEnd); joy.addEventListener('pointercancel', joyEnd); joy.addEventListener('lostpointercapture', joyEnd);
```
Knob default transform none; set '' maybe. Use translate(0,0).

Touch buttons:
```js
function bindHold(el, fn){
 el.addEventListener('pointerdown', e=>{ e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); el.classList.add('pressed'); fn(); });
 const up = ()=> el.classList.remove('pressed');
 el.addEventListener('pointerup', up); el.addEventListener('pointercancel', up); el.addEventListener('pointerleave', up);
}
bindHold(btnJump, ()=>{ wantJump=true; });
bindHold(btnBreak, breakTarget);
bindHold(btnPlace, placeBlock);
```
Using pointerleave may remove pressed; fine.

Ensure these buttons don't cause body click/start overlay. stopPropagation.

Hotbar click:
```js
slotEls.forEach((el,i)=> el.addEventListener('click', e=>{ e.preventDefault(); selectSlot(i); }));
```
Click may also trigger overlay? overlay hidden during play. fine. On mobile, click from touch after pointerup; fine.

Overlay:
```js
startBtn.addEventListener('click', e=>{ e.stopPropagation(); beginPlay(); });
overlay.addEventListener('click', e=>{ if (e.target.closest('button')) return; beginPlay(); });
resetBtn.addEventListener('click', e=>{ e.stopPropagation(); resetWorld(); beginPlay(); });
```
beginPlay after reset: on mobile sets playing; on desktop requests lock again. Fine.

visibilitychange: if hidden clear keys and wantJump.

Resize:
```js
function onResize(){
 camera.aspect=innerWidth/innerHeight;
 camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
 renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio||1,2));
 renderer.setSize(innerWidth,innerHeight);
}
window.addEventListener('resize', onResize);
```
Orientation change triggers resize.

Animation:
```js
let last=performance.now(), bobPhase=0, elapsed=0;
function animate(){
 requestAnimationFrame(animate);
 const now=performance.now();
 let dt=(now-last)/1000; last=now;
 if (dt>0.1) dt=0.1;
 elapsed += dt;

 if (playing) updatePlayer(dt);
 else { // idle: settle? no
 }

 // camera
 const speed = Math.hypot(player.vel.x, player.vel.z);
 if (playing && player.grounded && speed>0.4) bobPhase += dt*(6+speed*1.1);
 const bob = playing && player.grounded ? Math.sin(bobPhase)*Math.min(speed*0.006,0.035) : 0;
 camera.position.set(player.pos.x, player.pos.y+EYE+bob, player.pos.z);
 camera.rotation.x = pitch;
 camera.rotation.y = yaw;
 camera.rotation.z = 0;

 updateTarget();
 updateParticles(dt);

 // grow
 for (i=growQueue.length-1;...){ mesh.scale = min(1, scale+dt*5); if >=1 set 1 and remove }
 // clouds
 for (const c of clouds) { c.group.position.x += c.speed*dt; if (c.group.position.x>75) c.group.position.x=-75; }
 // water
 water.position.y = 2.15 + Math.sin(elapsed*0.7)*0.012;
 water.material.opacity = 0.8 + Math.sin(elapsed*0.9)*0.025;

 renderer.render(scene,camera);
}
animate();
```
Camera position even when paused: remains. Should animate rendering continuously. Good.

Important: `updateTarget` uses `playing`; when paused, hides highlight. Fine.

`growQueue` handling: scale increment by dt*5 from 0.5 to 1 in 0.1s.

FPS? no.

Initial camera positioning before first frame: animate runs immediately and positions camera. Good.

Check sunGlow position: at z=-126, camera far 600; sky sphere radius 320 centered origin; sun at distance 167 inside sky. Good.

Water plane 650 wide at y=2.15, extends beyond sky sphere? Half-width 325 > sphere 320 at horizon; fine, fog hides.

One issue: `sky` sphere is centered at origin and scene.fog doesn't apply. Camera near origin; fine.

Culling: water plane big, draw fine.

Shadow camera ±24 covers island 0..16 and trees. Good.

Potential shadow acne on flat ground: bias -0.0006. Fine.

Now init call. Also maybe set `document.body.classList.add('playing')` only when playing.

One more: pointer lock request might throw a promise rejection warning in console. In r128 `requestPointerLock` returns undefined or promise in newer browsers; use `const p = ...; if (p && p.catch) p.catch(()=>{})`.

Also `unadjustedMovement` not needed.

