`body.touch #hotbar` at line 216 comes before the landscape media at 221; same specificity, later landscape wins. Good. But at width>720 and touch (tablet landscape 1024x768), `body.touch #hotbar` sets 202px, which is quite high. On tablets, the controls are at bottom corners and hotbar could well be at 18px center, since tablet width is large enough to avoid overlap (hotbar 450px wide vs controls at edges). For a 1024 wide tablet, centered hotbar 470? Slots 54 desktop (unless width≤720, not applied) => 8*54+7*6+14 = 488, occupies x 268..756; joystick at 18..134, action buttons at right 900..1000; no overlap. So 18px is fine. But `isCoarse` true on tablet, so `body.touch #hotbar` puts it at 202 unnecessarily. Need to restrict to max-width 720. Use `@media (max-width:720px){ body.touch #hotbar { bottom: 202px } }` rather than global. Let's move it inside the media query. And keep the landscape override.

Change line 216 to be inside media at line 215 before close:
```css
        body.touch #hotbar { bottom: calc(202px + ...); }
    }
```
Then remove the standalone line. Also toast at 268 on a narrow non-touch desktop is high; but toast only appears on actions and a narrow desktop window would be unusual. Better scope toast to `body.touch` too, or leave. The toast at 268 is above the hotbar at 18 in a narrow desktop, floating high. Not a big deal but let's scope:
```css
@media(max-width:720px){ #toast{ bottom: calc(180px...) } body.touch #toast { bottom: calc(268px...) } ...}
```
Simpler: inside media, `body.touch #toast { bottom: calc(268px...); }`, and keep `#toast` default 104. On narrow desktop, default 104 (above hotbar 18+56=74), good. On mobile, 268. Do that.

And `body.touch #hotbar` inside media.

